"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[4952],{23898:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"new","desc":"Creates an animal pen.\\n\\nSeeds the replica with an empty pen (no eggs, no animals, no drops) at\\n`penConfig.maxCapacity`, then hands off to [PropBaseClass.new] with the\\n`CollectItems` client allowlist.\\n\\nWhen restoring from a save on the server, the saved props are first replayed\\nforward through [AnimalPenBaseClass:_calculateRetroactiveDrops] so the pen\\nreflects what it would have produced while the owner was away.\\n\\nRealm-specific setup afterwards:\\n\\n- **Server** \u2014 starts the drop timer and the hatching timer.\\n- **Client** \u2014 starts the egg/animal/drop visualization. The owner also gets\\n  the collection UI, deferred until building finishes if the pen is still\\n  under construction.","params":[{"name":"propData","desc":"","lua_type":"PropData"},{"name":"penConfig","desc":"`maxAnimals` and `maxCapacity`","lua_type":"PropTypes.AnimalPenConfig"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"AnimalPen"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":184,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_calculateRetroactiveDrops","desc":"Replays a pen\'s idle production forward from the moment it was last saved, so\\na returning player finds the pen in the state it *would* have been in had the\\nserver never stopped. Called once, from the constructor, before anything\\nstarts ticking.\\n\\nReturns a new props table; it does not mutate `savedProps`.\\n\\n### What it computes\\n\\n**1. Retroactive hatching.** Any egg whose `placedAt + hatchTime` has already\\npassed is converted into an animal, exactly as the live hatching timer would\\nhave. The new animal\'s `spawnedAt` and `lastDropTime` are backdated to\\n`hatchAt`, not to now \u2014 so an egg that hatched early in a long absence goes on\\nto earn credit for the rest of that absence in step 2. Hatching is resolved\\nbefore drops are computed, for that reason.\\n\\n**2. Retroactive drops.** For each animal (including the ones just hatched),\\n`floor(timeSinceLastDrop / dropInterval)` is how many drops it *should* have\\nproduced. Those are added one at a time so the running total can be checked\\nagainst `capacity` on every single one, and the loop stops the moment the pen\\nis full.\\n\\n### Deliberate design choices\\n\\n- **Capacity truncates the payout, and the remainder is discarded.** Every\\n  animal\'s `lastDropTime` is reset to now unconditionally at the end \u2014\\n  including animals whose drops were cut short by a full pen, and including\\n  the sub-interval remainder of a partially elapsed cycle. Idle time therefore\\n  pays out at most `maxCapacity` no matter how long the absence was, and does\\n  not \\"bank\\" anything. This is what keeps a pen worth returning to, and it is\\n  also what stops a long absence from instantly refilling the pen again on the\\n  next tick.\\n- **The cap applies across the whole pen, not per animal.** Drops are counted\\n  in aggregate before the loop and incremented as they are added, so animals\\n  processed earlier in iteration order can consume the whole allowance. Since\\n  `animals` is a hash map, which animal \\"wins\\" is not deterministic \u2014 an\\n  acceptable trade because drops of different types are interchangeable at the\\n  capacity level.\\n- **Missing config is skipped loudly, not fatally.** An animal whose item data\\n  has no `penData` warns and is passed over rather than aborting the whole\\n  replay, so one bad item id cannot cost a player their entire pen.","params":[{"name":"savedProps","desc":"Persisted pen state","lua_type":"PropTypes.SavedAnimalPenData"},{"name":"penConfig","desc":"Fallback limits when the save has none","lua_type":"PropTypes.AnimalPenConfig"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Caught-up copy of the pen state","lua_type":"PropTypes.SavedAnimalPenData"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":346,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_startCollectionTimer","desc":"Starts the `Stepped` loop that produces drops. Runs for the life of the prop;\\nowned by `collectionMaid`.\\n\\nEach tick every animal whose `dropInterval` has elapsed since its\\n`lastDropTime` contributes one drop. Drops are accumulated into a local table\\nfirst and only then applied via [AnimalPenBaseClass:_addDropWithData], and the\\nanimal timers are persisted in one replica write at the end \u2014 so a pen full of\\nanimals dropping on the same frame costs a bounded number of replica updates\\nrather than one per animal.\\n\\nCapacity is enforced downstream in `_addDropWithData`, so a full pen still\\nadvances `lastDropTime` and simply discards the drop.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":520,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_startHatchingTimer","desc":"Starts the `Stepped` loop that hatches incubating eggs. Runs for the life of\\nthe prop; owned by `collectionMaid`.\\n\\nAn egg whose `placedAt + hatchTime` has passed is replaced by a random animal\\nfrom its `hatchableAnimalItemIds` \u2014 hatch outcome is rolled at hatch time, not\\nat purchase time. The animal is added via\\n[AnimalPenBaseClass:_addHatchedAnimal] and the egg is removed.\\n\\nEach write re-reads `props` immediately before cloning it, because the drop\\ntimer runs on the same step and would otherwise be clobbered by a stale copy.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":592,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"CollectItems","desc":"Client-callable entry point for emptying the pen \u2014 allow-listed in\\n`_allowedClientFunctions`, so it is reached via `DispatchRemoteEvent`. The\\nclient calls it both from the collect prompt and automatically when the owner\\nwalks inside the pen\'s radius.\\n\\nVerifies ownership, then clears `drops`, stamps `lastCollectionTime`, and\\nfires `Collected` with the collected table \u2014 that signal is what the\\ninventory layer credits from.\\n\\nEvery animal\'s `lastDropTime` is also reset to now, so collecting restarts the\\nproduction cycle rather than letting a partially-elapsed interval pay out\\nimmediately afterwards.\\n\\nNo-ops when the pen is empty, so a spurious call costs nothing.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"The requesting client","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":672,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_addDropWithData","desc":"Adds one drop of `itemId`, respecting `capacity`, and fires `AddedDrop`.\\n\\nDrops are stored as one entry per item id with a `quantity`, so a pen holding\\ntwenty of the same resource is one replica entry rather than twenty.\\n\\nIdentical to [AnimalPenBaseClass:AddDrop] except that it re-reads `props`\\nimmediately before writing instead of trusting a caller-held copy. That is why\\nthe production timer uses this one: it runs on the same step as the hatching\\ntimer, and a stale read would drop hatched animals on the floor.","params":[{"name":"itemId","desc":"Item to add one of","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":730,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"AddDrop","desc":"Adds one drop of `itemId` to the pen, respecting `capacity`, and fires\\n`AddedDrop`. The public entry point for granting a pen drop from outside the\\nproduction timer \u2014 rewards, admin commands, and so on.\\n\\nSilently no-ops when the pen is already at capacity. Use\\n[AnimalPenBaseClass:_addDropBypassCapacity] when the drop must not be lost.\\n\\n:::note\\nCurrently unreferenced \u2014 the production timer uses the internal\\n`_addDropWithData` instead. Kept as the supported way for other systems to\\ngrant a pen drop.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"itemId","desc":"Item to add one of","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"_origin","desc":"Accepted but unused; drop placement is chosen client-side","lua_type":"CFrame?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":801,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_addDropBypassCapacity","desc":"Adds a drop that must not be lost to a full pen.\\n\\nRather than exceeding `capacity`, it makes room: when the pen is full it\\nevicts one existing drop \u2014 preferring one whose item id looks like an egg,\\nfalling back to any entry \u2014 and then adds the new one, keeping the total at\\nthe cap. If nothing can be evicted it gives up and adds nothing.\\n\\nIntended for outcomes the player has already \\"earned\\" and would consider lost\\nif silently dropped, such as a hatched animal arriving into a pen that filled\\nup with ordinary resources while they were away.\\n\\n:::note\\nCurrently unreferenced. [AnimalPenBaseClass:_addHatchedAnimal] writes into\\n`animals` directly rather than routing through the drops table, so nothing\\nexercises this path today. It is kept as the intended escape hatch for\\ncapacity-exempt grants.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"itemId","desc":"Item to add one of","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":876,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_addHatchedAnimal","desc":"Records a newly hatched animal in `props.animals` under a fresh\\n`animal_<random>` key, with its drop timer starting now and a random yaw if\\nthe caller did not supply one.\\n\\nAnimals live in their own table rather than in `drops`, so they are **not**\\nsubject to `capacity` \u2014 the egg was already gated against `maxAnimals` when it\\nwas placed, and that is where the limit is enforced.\\n\\nOnly data is written here. The client spawns the visual model in response to\\nthe `props` change.","params":[{"name":"animalItemId","desc":"Item id of the animal that hatched","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"origin","desc":"Pen-relative spot the egg sat at","lua_type":"{ X: number, Y: number, Z: number, R: number? }"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":967,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"AddProduct","desc":"Places an egg into the pen to incubate. Server-only: it is kept off\\n`_allowedClientFunctions`, since spending the egg is the caller\'s job.\\n\\nVerifies ownership, that `productItemId` really is an `AnimalEgg`, and that\\nthe offset is inside the pen. It then enforces `maxAnimals` against\\n**eggs plus animals combined**, so a player cannot queue eggs past the pen\'s\\neventual animal limit.\\n\\nOn success the egg is stored with its `placedAt` timestamp, the egg type\'s\\n`hatchTime`, and a random yaw; the hatching timer takes it from there.\\nConsuming the egg from the player\'s inventory is the caller\'s responsibility.\\n\\nEvery rejection is a silent no-op: the server path that calls it acts on a\\nclient request the UI should already have prevented.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"The requesting client","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"productItemId","desc":"Item id of the egg being placed","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"offset","desc":"Pen-relative X/Z offset in studs","lua_type":"Vector2"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1038,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_isOffsetWithinBounds","desc":"Whether a pen-relative offset falls inside the bounding box footprint.\\n`offset.Y` is the **Z** axis in world space.\\n\\nReached from both realms \u2014 the server uses it to validate egg placement, the\\nclient to validate an egg\'s stored position before rendering it.","params":[{"name":"offset","desc":"Pen-relative X/Z offset in studs","lua_type":"Vector2"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":1124,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_isOffsetTooCloseToExistingProducts","desc":"Whether placing an egg at `newOffset` would land within 1.5 studs of an\\nexisting egg. The spacing is a bare literal here rather than a `BaseData`\\nconstant, unlike the equivalent crop spacing on [Soil].\\n\\n:::note\\nCurrently unreferenced \u2014 [AnimalPenBaseClass:AddProduct] checks bounds and the\\nanimal cap but not spacing, so eggs may currently be stacked on the same spot.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"newOffset","desc":"Candidate pen-relative offset","lua_type":"Vector2"}],"returns":[{"desc":"`true` means the spot is blocked","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1164,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_setupCollectionUI","desc":"Builds the owner-only collection UI and the two ways of collecting. Everything\\nit creates is owned by `collectionMaid`.\\n\\nThe UI is a cloned `Assets.UI.Collection` billboard adorned to an attachment\\n3.5 studs above the pen, parented to PlayerGui and shown only while the custom\\nProximityPrompt is in range. The prompt is suppressed entirely while the\\nplayer has a prop selected in placement mode, so collecting cannot fight with\\nediting.\\n\\nCollection happens two ways, both funnelling into a `CollectItems` dispatch:\\nexplicitly via the prompt or the on-screen button, and implicitly via a\\nthrottled proximity poll (every `PROXIMITY_CHECK_INTERVAL`) that auto-collects\\nwhen the owner walks within half the pen\'s bounding-box magnitude. Both check\\nfor drops first so an empty pen sends nothing.\\n\\nTwo progress bars track the pen\'s caps \u2014 \\"Products\\" (`drops` against\\n`capacity`) and \\"Animals\\" (`animals + eggs` against `maxAnimals`) \u2014 each\\ndriven by its own replica listener. Both force-set rather than tween whenever\\nthe bar is shrinking or the UI is hidden, so a bar never animates downward\\nfrom a stale value the player never saw.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1221,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_setupProductVisualization","desc":"Installs every listener that turns replicated pen state into instances. Runs\\nfor all clients, not just the owner; everything it spawns is owned by\\n`productMaid`.\\n\\nThree streams, tracked by three separate local tables:\\n\\n- **Eggs** (`props.eggs`) \u2014 each new egg spawns its model at the stored\\n  pen-relative origin plus a \\"Hatching\\" progress bar, refreshed every\\n  RenderStep. Eggs the server has removed are torn down along with their bar.\\n- **Animals** (`props.animals`) \u2014 each animal id is spawned once and then\\n  remembered in `spawnedAnimals`, because the `props` listener fires for\\n  unrelated changes too and would otherwise duplicate models. Animals are\\n  scattered randomly within the middle half of the pen, put on the animal\\n  collision group so they do not shove the player, and tagged\\n  `AnimalData.MODEL_TAG` for whatever drives their wandering.\\n- **Drops** (`drops`) \u2014 visuals are reconciled against `quantity` per item id\\n  via `visualizedCounts`, spawning only the difference rather than rebuilding.\\n  When the drops table goes empty \u2014 the client\'s cue that a collection was\\n  accepted \u2014 every resource visual is destroyed with a particle burst and its\\n  count reset. Animals deliberately survive that sweep: they are permanent\\n  residents, not collectibles.\\n\\nFinally it back-fills visuals for everything already present when the pen\\nstreamed in.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1445,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_calculateProductOrigin","desc":"Converts an egg\'s stored pen-relative origin into a world CFrame, relative to\\nthe model\'s `PrimaryPart`. Returns `nil` when the model is not built or the\\noffset no longer falls inside the pen \u2014 the latter being possible if the pen\\nwas swapped for a smaller one after the egg was placed.","params":[{"name":"origin","desc":"Stored egg origin","lua_type":"{ X: number, Y: number, Z: number, R: number? }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"CFrame?"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1820,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"PropData","desc":"[PropBaseClass.PropData] with the persisted props narrowed to the pen schema\\n(`eggs`, `animals`, `drops`, `lastCollectionTime`, `capacity`). All other\\nfields are inherited unchanged.","fields":[{"name":"savedPropData","lua_type":"BaseUtil.SavedPropData","desc":"With `props` narrowed to `SavedAnimalPenData`"}],"source":{"line":113,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"AnimalPen","desc":"Instance shape of an animal pen, on top of everything inherited from\\n[PropBaseClass].\\n\\n`collectionMaid` doubles as the server\'s timer owner, so destroying the prop\\nstops production on both realms.","fields":[{"name":"clientReplica","lua_type":"ReplicaClient","desc":"Replica narrowed to `AnimalPenReplicaData` (client)"},{"name":"serverReplica","lua_type":"ReplicaServer","desc":"Replica narrowed to `AnimalPenReplicaData` (server)"},{"name":"collectionPrompt","lua_type":"ProximityPrompt?","desc":"Custom-styled collect prompt (owner\'s client)"},{"name":"ui","lua_type":"BillboardGui?","desc":"Collection UI: interact button plus two progress bars"},{"name":"collectionMaid","lua_type":"Maid","desc":"Owns the collection UI and the server timers"},{"name":"_penConfig","lua_type":"PropTypes.AnimalPenConfig","desc":"`maxAnimals` / `maxCapacity` from item data"},{"name":"productMaid","lua_type":"Maid","desc":"Owns every spawned egg, animal and drop visual"},{"name":"AddedDrop","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"(itemId) \u2014 server-side, one drop was produced"},{"name":"Collected","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"({ [string]: DropEntry }) \u2014 server-side, drops were collected"}],"source":{"line":138,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}}],"name":"AnimalPenBaseClass","desc":"Base class for every animal pen. Extends [PropBaseClass]; concrete pens are\\ncreated through [AnimalPen], which reads the pen\'s capacity limits out of item\\ndata and passes them down as an `AnimalPenConfig`.\\n\\n### The economy loop\\n\\nA pen runs a small idle-production chain:\\n\\n```\\negg placed \u2192 incubates for `hatchTime` \u2192 hatches into a random animal\\n           \u2192 animal drops an item every `dropInterval`\\n           \u2192 drops accumulate up to `maxCapacity`\\n           \u2192 owner walks into the pen (or triggers the prompt) to collect\\n```\\n\\nTwo independent caps govern it. `maxAnimals` limits *eggs + animals* combined\\nand is checked when an egg is placed, so a pen cannot be over-subscribed by\\nqueuing eggs. `maxCapacity` limits *uncollected drops*; once reached,\\nproduction simply stops until the owner collects. That stall is the design\\nintent \u2014 the cap is what makes collecting worth doing and what makes larger\\npens worth buying.\\n\\n### Naming\\n\\nThe persisted schema calls the incubating items `eggs` and the code calls them\\n\\"products\\" in places; they are the same thing. Likewise `drops` holds both\\nresource drops and hatched animals \u2014 an animal reaching the pen is modelled as\\na drop that happens to render as a walking model instead of a collectible.\\n\\n### Realms\\n\\nThe server owns all state and runs two `Stepped` timers (drop production and\\nhatching), writing everything through the inherited Replica\'s `props` key. The\\nclient owns visuals: it spawns egg models with hatching progress bars, spawns\\nanimal and resource models as they appear in replicated data, and drives the\\ncollection UI. Only `CollectItems` is client-callable; `AddProduct` leaves\\nspending the egg to its caller, so only the server calls it.\\n\\n### Offline progress\\n\\nBecause timers only run while the server does, pen state loaded from a save is\\nreplayed forward by [AnimalPenBaseClass:_calculateRetroactiveDrops] before the\\nreplica is created.\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].BaseEnabled \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks\\nenable it deliberately.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","tags":["dormant"],"source":{"line":55,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/AnimalPenBaseClass.luau"}}')}}]);